__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
o.txt
gpu_out.txt
amort*.log
bench_gpu.log
run_*.log
# ...except this one. It is the console record of the full-scale 3-seed RL run
# (3 x 2000 iters x 4096 envs) that the reported 80.4 +/- 4.9% headroom and
# rho = +0.991 come from. That script printed without saving arrays, so this
# log is the only artefact of the run and the README cites it directly.
!sim/run_final.log

# papers are third-party PDFs; not ours to redistribute
papers/**/*.pdf

# Trained weights are large and regenerable; results arrays are NOT ignored.
# The .npz/.npy results total ~84 kB and the Colab notebook needs them after a
# fresh clone, so a reviewer can see the 26-minute and GPU experiments without
# re-running them. Regenerate with sim/gen_figdata*.py.
# Trained weights: the two below are tiny (42 kB + 38 kB) and ARE committed,
# so the notebook can run live network inference and live RL rollouts after a
# fresh clone. Any other pickle (optimiser state, checkpoints) stays ignored.
sim/*.pkl
!sim/amort_hard_theta.pkl
!sim/rl_policy.pkl

# --- kept local, not published -------------------------------------------
# submission/ holds the four deliverable PDFs and nothing else, so a reader
# sees exactly what was submitted. Everything used to BUILD them -- LaTeX
# sources, the Markdown originals, the generated table fragments they \input,
# the drafting pipeline and the internal checklist -- lives in submission_src/
# and is not published. Nothing is deleted; it is all still on disk, and older
# versions remain in git history.
submission_src/
figures/tables*.tex
# Fig0c was the single-column architecture variant; no document uses it.
figures/Fig0c_architecture_1col.*
